Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(worker-isolation): close+reap the child's Chromium
 before returning the browser permit; opt-in batch stop rule S4

processor.ts (isolated children only; non-isolated path unchanged):
- getSharedBrowser registers each launched Chromium and its process group.
- releaseBrowserSlot -> releaseChildBrowserPermit: when the last holder in the
  child releases, every browser is detached, closed, and its process group is
  confirmed gone (close -> wait -> SIGKILL group -> wait) BEFORE remoteRelease.
  Unconfirmed cleanup withholds the permit and opens the child's browser
  circuit; the parent reaps on exit (existing quarantine path).
- retireChildBrowser: with no pid handle only a COMPLETED close() counts;
  a timed-out/failed close no longer releases the permit.
- pdfRecovery: re-check the circuit after resetBrowserCircuit().

worker.ts + lib/batch-stop-rule.ts: BATCH_STOP_RULE_FAILED_JOBS (unset/0 =
inert). After failJob records a failure, count distinct failed jobs in the
batch; at >= N (or any retry-exhausted job) run the POST /batch/cancel sequence
(flag -> purge -> snapshot -> PG cancel) and skip the retry re-enqueue.

Tests: browser-close-order.test.ts (real isolated children + Chromium; asserts
no live Chromium at every permit return on success / failure / cancellation /
child-death paths), batch-stop-rule.test.ts (default inert, threshold N trips,
cancel sequence order, batch-1276 simulation).
